{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391874-the-one-support-spell-against-werewolves","id":1391874,"title":"The one support spell against werewolves.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-27T00:07:06-07:00","id":1391874,"title":"The one support spell against werewolves.","content":"Ok, on my next session, the characters would face a group of werewolves. They'll be buying time while a master concludes a ritual, and for them to do that, that master will cast a single spell to support them so they, you know, dont end up torn to pieces. <br /> <br /> Now, the master spheres are...<br /> <br /> Prime 5<br /> Correspondence 5<br /> Spirit 5<br /> Entropy 1<br /> Forces 3<br /> Matter 2<br /> Mind 3<br /> Time 3<br /> Life 3 <br /> <br /> She'll be using her last 3 points of Quintessence, so it must be a immediate effect (no ritual) with a plausible difficulty, so she can cover at least 3 of them (dividing successes rule). The idea of the whole scene is for the players to feel they're running out of time (not something like I'll teleport you out of here in the most vulgar and anticlimactic way possible)<br /> <br /> What would you cast under those conditions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T04:39:10-07:00","id":1391894,"title":"","content":"Between correspondence, spirit and life you can make a pretty decent ward vs werewolfs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T05:26:15-07:00","id":1391900,"title":"","content":"Correspondence 3/Life 3/Matter 2/Prime 2. Fill the lungs of all the werewolves with pure silver. Problem solved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T07:42:13-07:00","id":1391931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391874-the-one-support-spell-against-werewolves?p=1391900#post1391900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correspondence 3/Life 3/Matter 2/Prime 2. Fill the lungs of all the werewolves with pure silver. Problem solved.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True, but I want the characters to deal with the werewolves, not the npc to solve everything (maybe I wasnt clear on that: the master I mentioned is an npc). Thats why the rote is to support the characters, not to solve the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T10:07:40-07:00","id":1391983,"title":"","content":"It seems like it's the Master's situation, and she has the abilities to solve it herself without putting less powerful mages in danger. She can create a ward, conjure protective spirits, or both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T11:13:57-07:00","id":1392001,"title":"","content":"With Correspondence 5, the Master can wall herself off from surrounding reality completely. The werewolves won't even be able to perceive her, let alone interact with her. You should tweak your scenario a bit so that there's a genuine need for the characters to be present. The race against time is a cool concept, but Master-level mages are insanely powerful and can ignore or shrug of most threats with ease.<br /> <br /> What about something that neutralises the Master during the ritual? Maybe a Paradox Spirit shows up and she has to spend all her time using Prime 5 to deal with it, leaving the PCs to hold off the werewolves until she's done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T11:43:04-07:00","id":1392008,"title":"","content":"Might be hard for the master to kill all the werewolves directly if there are enough werewolves and possible spirit protection might complicate matters. <br /> <br /> Teleporting away seems like a temporary solution. <br /> <br /> So... I would cast a long lasting single area werewolf ward (the ban type ward that makes force irrelevant) in the form of planes that separate the area into maybe 5 foot long and wide, 10 foot tall spaces that werecreatures and disembodied/non-human spirits can't cross that also prevents spirit world travel. So the werewolves will be trapped in spaces and the mages can ranged kill them with silver and fire. Correspondence 3 (4 in M20), spirit 2, life 2 I think<br /> <br /> Or for a bit cheaper, magically, I could just fill the air in a large area with silver using prime 2, matter2, correspondence 2 (like as far as the horizon, like 3 miles). Maybe I'd add prime if I'm not sure about silver and werewolves just to reinforce the reality of silver killing werewolves. <br /> <br /> Then the mages just have to survive for a bit as the werewolves die in rage and agony... Actually, maybe that earlier idea of a ward of protection against wolves would be the first thing to cast, then I can silverize the air at my leisure.<br /> <br /> Hmmm. I'm straying from the initial Idea. I'll think on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T12:18:49-07:00","id":1392016,"title":"","content":"An immediate effect (no ritual) that actually worksagainst such a dangerous threat, and helps others, it's a very peculiar requisite.<br /> <br /> As has been said, this Master seems better prepared to handle things himself OR summon something that does...simply because this magick it's usually <i>easier </i>(and more effective) than empowering others is when you're short on time and need to make the most of your Arete roll. A very <i>peculiar </i>situation needs to be going on to make this the best choice...<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Have you tought about handling the mages Charms instead? These can be as potent as needed for the plot (assumed to be built beforehand) and, since you expend them, they won't save your ass for very long.<br /> Maybe some sort of regeneration item that can bring a mage from death but only a few times, or a forcefield that only resist a certain amount of damage, something like that could give the feeling of not having enough &quot;living space&quot;... These could be handled to the trusty cabal while the Master works on the important ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-27-2020, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T12:21:06-07:00","id":1392017,"title":"","content":"I know, I'll use time 3 and correspondence 3 and forces or mind to retroactively call for help, causing some people in the past to turn this place into a werewolf killing trap!<br /> <br /> More seriously, maybe the master isn't imaginative enough for that odd ward I mentioned earlier and just ensures each person is warded against werewolves and spirits (including direct spirit effects like gifts and charms) and solid matter. Like a spherical force field with one side beneath the mage's feet and the rest mostly beyond arm's reach.<br /> <br /> Edit: then again, that seems to kinda make the werewolves not very threatening....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 05-27-2020, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T12:27:46-07:00","id":1392021,"title":"","content":"How about a prime spirit mind forces 3 comprehensive illusion that will make the mages seem like werewolves of the same pack that they've known for a while, and the mages now have to lead the werewolves on some wild goose chase so the master can conduct the ritual in peace?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T12:32:29-07:00","id":1392023,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'd keep it simple and have the master use Time 3 to give everyone more actions for the combat. Werewolves can spend Rage to do so. It lets the PCs dodge and still do something. It levels the playing field without being TOO helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T12:45:00-07:00","id":1392027,"title":"","content":"@florin: My only worry is that would probably need more successes than the wards","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T13:15:59-07:00","id":1392034,"title":"","content":"True. With splitting successes, you'll need to add 3 successes to target 3 people for a scene. That means at minimum you'll need 5 to add 1 action per round. Granted you'll be rolling against a difficulty of 3 with Quintessence expenditure, assuming the master's magick is coincidental in the area. So, there's a CHANCE it would work, but not a great chance. But since it's an NPC, I as an ST would just say the effect works and let the PCs have some Time-magick-enhanced fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T12:47:06-07:00","id":1392281,"title":"","content":"You have provided amazing ideas. Thank you so much!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T12:53:12-07:00","id":1392286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391874-the-one-support-spell-against-werewolves?p=1392034#post1392034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. With splitting successes, you'll need to add 3 successes to target 3 people for a scene. That means at minimum you'll need 5 to add 1 action per round. Granted you'll be rolling against a difficulty of 3 with Quintessence expenditure, assuming the master's magick is coincidental in the area. So, there's a CHANCE it would work, but not a great chance. But since it's an NPC, I as an ST would just say the effect works and let the PCs have some Time-magick-enhanced fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You hit the point. Most of the &quot;master dealing with that personally WHILE conducting the ritual&quot; seems to require many successes, considering there would be at least 3 werewolves there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T14:06:01-07:00","id":1392308,"title":"","content":"How combat capable is your mage team? If they're powerfully optimized in that regard (having good combat pools and scary combat rotes), an extra action a turn will allow them to survive a werewolf onslaught. If not, you might want to consider more powerful protection, like a small area forces 3 (for area of effect of force shield), correspondence 3 (4 in M20), spirit 3, life 3 spirit and werewolf ban for a scene for 4 successes. The field would be stuck in an area of several dozen square yards and would not protect against the werewolf just flinging objects at players or swatting them with mundane melee weapons. Maybe the ward could have been made more powerful but the master didn't have enough successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T17:20:39-07:00","id":1392363,"title":"","content":"Conjure up an illusion of Kristen Stewart's dead-eyed teen from the <i>Twilight</i> movies so all the werewolves are too concerned with stripping off their shirts and posing to interfere with the ritual?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T18:46:16-07:00","id":1392379,"title":"","content":"I think the biggest question is how formidable the players are. A party of, undoubtedly, prepared Mage that know an attack might be coming may not need a whole lot of help with 3 werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T05:03:42-07:00","id":1392479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391874-the-one-support-spell-against-werewolves?p=1392379#post1392379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the biggest question is how formidable the players are. A party of, undoubtedly, prepared Mage that know an attack might be coming may not need a whole lot of help with 3 werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>That.<br /> <br /> More so, if the Master knows what capabilities have the PC, what &quot;gimmicks&quot; they use to figth, you could focus on covering some flaw or weak spot in their usual strategy - casting something that synergizes with what the players can cast *migth* be easier than trying an all purpose solution","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T12:06:24-07:00","id":1392619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1391874-the-one-support-spell-against-werewolves?p=1392363#post1392363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conjure up an illusion of Kristen Stewart's dead-eyed teen from the <i>Twilight</i> movies so all the werewolves are too concerned with stripping off their shirts and posing to interfere with the ritual?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or said werewolves, insulted by the franchise, attack the illusion. Better yet, through in that teen and some sparkly vampires. . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T20:44:14-07:00","id":1392739,"title":"","content":"I suddenly want to make a mage that has a vampire detecting light that makes vampires sparkle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}